# GMS's readout ends "Final damage increases by 15% with each enemy pierced,
# and damage is doubled" -- one mechanic, not two: the arrow compounds x1.15
# per enemy, so the sixth takes 1.15^5 = 2.01x the first, which is the
# doubling. Dropped rather than averaged: an arrow that gains as it travels
# needs an order to travel along, and every enemy in reach takes the same
# damage here. An average would pay +46% on a full screen and nothing on one
# mob, which flatters the Crossbowman at mobbing for no reason it earned.
name: "Piercing Arrow"
skill_order: 1
description: "Fire an arrow through the enemies in front of you."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_CROSSBOWMAN
max_level: 20
base_delay_ms: 780
max_enemies: 6
lines: 4
base { skill_pct: 0.92 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.02 }
